    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12369366/comment/12495909",
          "id": "12495909",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Mirco,\nThe 'modality' of the response handling logic in HttpClient is a well know and a very old problem that dates back to the days of HttpClient 1.x. (I remember discussing the issue as early as year 2002). The problem has been resolved in HttpClient 4.0 codeline. I do not see a possibility for fixing  the problem in HttpClient 3.x without taking a very high risk of breaking existing applications.\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2007-05-15T09:11:51.840+0000",
          "updated": "2007-05-15T09:11:51.840+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12369366/comment/12495910",
          "id": "12495910",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "We will improve the API doc.\n\nI agree it's arguable if the response should be buffered at all in getResponseBodyAsString. Anyway, the buffered body is eligible for gc as soon as you release the reference to the method object.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
